Follow-up to the A+B+D staleness-audit PR. These are the Severity-C findings —
module docstrings that silently omitted substantial functionality the code
grew since they were written. Each addition was verified against the code path
it describes.

- cli: subcommand list covered 7 of the 27 registered verbs; rewritten to name
  the full set grouped by purpose, with `survey` as the primary analysis verb
  (`run` a deprecated alias, ADR-0042) and a pointer to the authoritative
  `subcommands` set in main().
- all_analyzers: was framed as a thin "facade"; it also houses the
  `run_all_analyzers` orchestrator (parallel dispatch, fingerprint stamp,
  file-presence filter, synthesis passes, edge dedup, manifest merge).
- tauri_ipc: added the 4th detection phase (Rust->TS emit/listen events ->
  event_publishes).
- wasm_bindgen: added the dynamic-WASM-load phase (WebAssembly.instantiate /
  .wasm URL imports / Emscripten -> imports edges to synthetic wasm modules);
  fixed the internal _create_wasm_load_edges docstring (wasm_load -> imports).
- di_resolution: documented the NestJS @Module registration edges (references,
  meta.mechanism=di_registration); fixed the stale link_di_resolution docstring.
- dataflow: documented the parallel Python-ast Tier-1 path annotate_dataflow_ast().
- crypto_flow: added ChaCha20Poly1305 to the Rust crate/write lists.
- annotation_convention: noted the 0.5 disambiguation_fallback for ambiguous
  @hg:dispatches targets (INV-zuhub), not just the 0.95 headline.
- d_lang: added field/variable/enum-member extraction and UFCS call-recovery
  (WI-situj / INV-vigaf) to the Detects list.
- rust_analyzer: added a Diagnostics section for the WI-todon UserWarning
  (zero scip-origin edges despite .rs files present).
- spec_validator: item-3 cross_field now names the other wired checks (ADR-0037
  is_resolved<->dst FK, origin_run_id FK, dangling-endpoint, confidence range,
  route-marker single-home, receiver-blind-magnet gate).

Docstring/comment-only; no behavior change.

